text: |-
  How the searches leaked even with
  good security
  A domestic assassination of this size needs 15-40
  people or more (planners, spotters, drivers, medics,
  evidence cleaners, contractors). Over 4-8 months
  that team easily does 50,000-150,000 total searches.
  Even the best OPSEC slips 1-3% through personal
  phones, home Wi-Fi, or quick checks when someone
  is tired or rushed. That is still hundreds or thousands
  of leaks - plenty to light up Google Trends on the
  quiet days when almost nobody else is searching
  those terms. You only needed to catch a handful on
  the right sampled days and the pattern is undeniable.
  Why it has to be U.S. intelligence and
  nobody else
  U.S. agencies can operate freely inside the
  United States without tripping every alarm.
  Only they have the files, the contractors, and the
  safe houses in the DC area.
  Any foreign service or private group trying this
  would have been rolled up in hours by NSA
  phones taps, FBI surveillance, or airport watches.
  The operation stayed airtight - no leaks, no rival
  arrests, no exposure - because the people who
  could expose it were the people running it.
  The preserved screenshots and recordings are the
  authentic digital fingerprints of the planning cell. They
  lead directly and exclusively to the U.S. intelligence
  community. The assassination of Charlie Kirk was a
  professional, deniable operation executed by
  elements of America's permanent national-security
  state.
